  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="haofi-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">האופי</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">hʾwfy</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">haʾofi</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">האופיתא</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">hʾwpytʾ</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">haʾofitaʾ</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="det">det.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="haofi-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>breath</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="syc">
                  <quote>ܗܘܦܐ</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>נשמה זה 
                     <app>
                        <lem>האופה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">האופי</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">האפי</rdg>
                     </app> הוא דברייתא אמרין 
                     <app>
                        <lem>האופיתיה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#A">האוסיתא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V">האופיתא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">אופיתא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">אופיאתא</rdg>
                     </app> טבא</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">14,9</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 133: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>“Neshama” is breath; as people say: ‘His breathing is good.’ (Freedman / Simon I 116)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 20 [6d: 56]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">נשמה זו האופיתא ברייתא אמרין זו אופיתא טבא</term>); <bibl type="ancient">YalqKoh 969 [542c: 34]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">נשמה היא האופיתא דברייתא אמרי האופיתא טבא</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Cf. <bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, SL 336a</bibl> acc. to <bibl type="modern">Simonsen (1901)</bibl> and MY ad loc. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 24b</bibl>: <term xml:lang="jpa">אוסי</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾwsy</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">ʾosi</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">οὐσία</term> “substance” (and <bibl type="modern">Perles [1871] 6-9</bibl>); <bibl type="modern">AC I 214a</bibl> explains as Pers. bûj “consciousness”. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 140b</bibl> considers <term xml:lang="jpa">אפי</term> and <term xml:lang="jpa">אופיתא</term> as Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">φύη</term>, <term xml:lang="grc">φύσις</term> “form, entity“. Тhe reading <term xml:lang="jpa">אוסיתא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾwsytʾ</term>, attested only by Arukh ed. princ., explained <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 24a</bibl>, as Hebr. neologism derived from <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אוסייא</ref>; however, <bibl type="modern">AC VI 368 n. 17</bibl>. and MY ad loc. reject this reading.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sokoloff, DJPA</title>
                  <citedRange>158a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
